## 65. CANONICAL DEFINITION

iRiel Memory is the personal continuity layer of the PRSL-AI Ecosystem responsible for preserving, organizing, retrieving, updating, distributing and forgetting information relevant to the user's Personal Intelligence Environment.

It operates under Privacy by Default, Local-First and Human-Controlled principles and remains independent from any specific device, AI model, provider or cloud infrastructure.


---

## 66. CANONICAL SHORT FORM

iRiel Memory:

Preserves continuity.
Not everything.

Remembers what matters.
Forgets what no longer matters.
Respects what is private.
Uses context to retrieve relevance.
Uses governance to control access.
Uses intelligent storage to manage placement.
Follows the user across authorized devices.
Remains independent from AI providers.
Remains independent from cloud infrastructure.

---

## 67. FOUNDATIONAL PRINCIPLE

The purpose of iRiel Memory is not to make the machine remember everything about the human.

Its purpose is to ensure that the human does not have to repeatedly rebuild their relationship with the machine.

Memory exists for continuity.

Continuity exists for the human.

The user remains the owner and authority of that continuity.


